            <div xml:id="d657">

                <pb facs="0518" n="510" sameAs="frus:frus1937v04/pg510"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">394.115 Panay/154: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hankow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-12-18T21:00:00+08:00">December 18, 1937—9
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 18—4:15 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>86. Following from Commander-in-Chief: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“0018. Boarding boat was Japanese motor launch, 40 feet long, engine
                            amidships, light machine gun in bow protected by steel shields. Boat’s
                            sides planking of clinker construction. Boat contained approximately 20
                            Japanese soldiers, boarding officers name previously reported to you by
                                <hi rendition="#italic">Panay</hi>.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>Sent to Department. Repeated to Peiping and Shanghai. Peiping repeat to
                    Tokyo.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
